# SOC2 audit engagement phase 2: Readiness Assessment (Gap Analysis) —
# Solace Cloud case study. One domain FRAGMENT of the shared
# solace-soc2-audit-cycle domain: this phase's 3 actions chain
# scoping-complete -> readiness-step1-done -> readiness-step2-done -> readiness-assessed,
# so the merged cycle plan can only reach this phase after Phase 1
# (Scoping & System Description) completes. 8-constraint split: every
# precondition/effect/goal here is a 1-conjunct (and ...) — far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 — and each action takes 1 parameter
# (PDDL8_MAX_PARAMS=8); soc2_test.rs asserts these bounds mechanically for
# every fragment (reusing crate::bench::togaf::verify_eight_constraint_split
# verbatim).
#
# COMPLIANCE-OVERCLAIM FENCE: no action effect below is named "compliant"
# or "opinion" — the audit ENGAGEMENT PROCESS is modeled here, never a
# compliance verdict. See packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl for the full
# fence disclosure.
#
# Public-ontology doctrine: the artifact node is a blank node; the phase is
# identified by its public SKOS notation. The only private predicate is
# the cng pipeline's ABI carrier ceng:pddlDomain (urn:chatman:engine#),
# disclosed in packs/soc2-audit-pack/ontology.ttl.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "AUDIT-READINESS" ;
    dcterms:description "Readiness Assessment (Gap Analysis) domain fragment of the solace-soc2-audit-cycle STRIPS domain."@en ;
    ceng:pddlDomain """
(define (domain solace-soc2-audit-cycle)
  (:requirements :strips)
  (:predicates
    (scoping-complete ?x)
    (readiness-step1-done ?x)
    (readiness-step2-done ?x)
    (readiness-assessed ?x))
  (:action inventory-existing-controls
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (scoping-complete ?x))
    :effect (and (readiness-step1-done ?x)))
  (:action perform-gap-analysis
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (readiness-step1-done ?x))
    :effect (and (readiness-step2-done ?x)))
  (:action produce-readiness-report
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (readiness-step2-done ?x))
    :effect (and (readiness-assessed ?x))))
""" .
